e rides it  will make  such a big difference and also seeing  the light at the end of the tunnel  leading towards summer there's real  concern about  vaccine hesitancy in black asian  minority ethnic  communities is that something you're  seeing  and what do you think we can do about it  just have these conversations bring the  light to people  i think it's good if people who have had  the vaccine discuss their experience  with it and then it will encourage  people who haven't  had the vaccine to understand what it  takes and  what the importance is of taking the  vaccine as well so i think what the main  goal is  all getting out of this together and  moving towards  normal times one conversation that you  have taken part in black lives matter  you took part in the march  in watford last year i wonder what you  think about wilfrid zaha saying  he's no longer going to take the knee  because he  considers it to be degrading do you see  where he's coming from  i feel like everyone's entitled to their  view so i have to understand where he's  coming from  because that's his own specific view and  i understand the people that do take  their knee as well because it's bringing  awareness to a situation that  people have been trying to fight for  many many years  it's just about unity not about because  this person chose one route and this  person chose another i don't appreciate  or respect them  it's just about respecting people for  their individual views and coming  together  and just understanding one another  person who wants to take a vaccine  respect you and person who doesn't  respect you come together and have a  conversation and we respect each other  for  our independent views yeah now the ioc  have said  no political protest and they consider  taking the need to be  a political gesture at the upcoming  olympics it's a global stage it's a  really powerful place  uh to make a statement what would you do  if if you were there this time around  it was something tha